  "author_guidance": "In the 24-round test these actors stopped being able to do anything (or never could): instructor (refused: move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True, move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True; the destination is the boundary's second place: was 'office', needed 'hangar', prepare-helicopter: you are the mechanic: was 'instructor', needed 'mechanic'; you are with the helicopter: was 'office', needed 'hangar'); mechanic (refused: drink-water: you are with the glass of water: was 'hangar', needed 'office', move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True; you are at the boundary's first place: was 'hangar', needed 'office', move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True; you are at the boundary's first place: was 'hangar', needed 'office'; the destination is the boundary's second place: was 'office', needed 'hangar'); sam (refused: move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True, move: the boundary is passable: was False, needed True; the destination is the boundary's second place: was 'office', needed 'hangar', practice-flight: you are with the helicopter: was 'office', needed 'hangar'). Every actor role must be able to act regularly: make sure some actor's action brings what each one's action needs to where it is checked (for example, if a carrier must hold goods before delivering, give another actor an action that loads goods onto the carrier, or let the carrier pick them up itself). A process may renew raw materials at their source or bring new demand, but never supply what an action makes or move goods between places. By the end of the 24-round test the only move still happening was request-training: the work stopped progressing. Make sure everything that can be taken or held can also be released or used up (for example a rule to put a shared tool back), and that each step's output is what the next step's checks need. In the 24-round test these moves were never possible for anyone: move (the boundary is passable: was False, needed True; nothing ever raises boundary.passable); practice-flight (you are with the helicopter: was 'office', needed 'hangar'). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that brings them there).",
